SUMMARY:Deadline: Prototype Fund Class 03 (Open-Source Software)
DESCRIPTION:Prototype Fund supports the development of socially relevant op
 en-source software\, offering low-threshold funding and coaching to indivi
 dual developers and small teams. ELIGIBILITY: individual developers or tea
 ms of up to four\; funded members must reside in the EU and the lead entit
 y must be based in Germany. Application window 1 October to 30 November 20
 26.\n\nOrganisation: Prototype Fund (Open Knowledge Foundation Germany)\nL
 ocation: Germany / EU (lead must be based in Germany\; funded members must
  reside in the EU)\nAward: Up to EUR 95\,000 over 6 months\, or up to EUR 
 158\,000 over 10 months\, plus coaching. No application fee.\nDuration: 6 
 or 10 months\n\nMore: https://www.prototypefund.de/en/application?utm_sour
 ce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.prototypefund.de/en/application?utm_source=artificialnouvea
 ugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Germany / EU (lead must be based in Germany\; funded members must 
 reside in the EU)
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:make-a-thek-mobility-knowledge-exchange-2026@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20261124T224215Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261201
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261202
SUMMARY:Deadline: make-a-thek: Mobility Scheme & Knowledge Exchange Program
 me (Europe + pilot countries)
DESCRIPTION:make-a-thek\, a Horizon Europe project (grant No. 101177660) co
 ordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\, connects creative spaces\, public
  libraries and makers across Europe and beyond to share skills in circular
  fashion\, traditional crafts and technology. Its open call runs two track
 s.\n\nOrganisation: make-a-thek (coordinated by Fab Lab Barcelona at IAAC\
 , funded by Horizon Europe)\nLocation: Various European pilot cities (Antw
 erp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Budapest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, R
 eykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)\; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early De
 c 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). Open to legal residents of EU member states
 \, Horizon Europe associated countries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, S
 outh Africa\, Indonesia\, Philippines and Chile.\nAward: Mobility Scheme: 
 EUR 1\,000 flat stipend for experienced practitioners. Knowledge Exchange 
 Programme: EUR 850 flat stipend. Up to 12 participants per track annually.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Short-term mobility: single events\, works
 hops or 2-day group meet-ups (Barcelona between end of November and start 
 of December 2026\; Berlin in May 2027).\n\nMore: https://www.makeathek.eu/
 opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.makeathek.eu/opencall?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk
 &utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Various European pilot cities (Antwerp\, Barcelona\, Berlin\, Buda
 pest\, Helsinki\, Kranj\, Milan\, Opole\, Reykjavik\, Kyiv\, Zaporizhzhia)
 \; meet-ups in Barcelona (late Nov/early Dec 2026) and Berlin (May 2027). 
 Open to legal residents of EU member states\, Horizon Europe associated co
 untries\, and the pilot countries Ghana\, South Africa\, Indonesia\, Phili
 ppines and Chile.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cerv-2026-citizens-rem@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261124T224215Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20270224T153000Z
DTEND:20270224T160000Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 17:00 CET: EU CERV: European Remembrance 2026-27 (CERV-202
 6-CITIZENS-REM)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 24 Feb 2027 at 17:00 CET.\n\nThe EU's main remembrance f
 unding line\, and emphatically not Holocaust-only: the 2026-27 call (cover
 ing both years\; there is no separate 2027 call) funds projects across fou
 r topics: 1) remembering democratic transitions and the (re)building of de
 mocratic institutions\; 2) remembrance of the Holocaust against Jewish peo
 ple\; 3) remembrance of the Holocaust\, acts of genocide\, war crimes and 
 crimes...\n\nOrganisation: European Commission / EACEA (Citizens\, Equalit
 y\, Rights and Values Programme)\nLocation: EU Member States (incl. OCTs) 
 and CERV-associated countries. Lead applicant must be a non-profit legal e
 ntity or international organisation.\nAward: EUR 50\,000 to EUR 500\,000 p
 er project\, from an estimated call budget of EUR 28 million (EUR 14M Holo
 caust remembrance of Jewish victims\; EUR 5M genocide\, war crimes and cri
 mes against humanity incl. Roma and LGBTIQ+ victims\; EUR 5M colonialism\,
  slavery and migration\; EUR 4M democratic transitions). No application fe
 e.\nDuration: Projects typically 12 to 24 months\n\nMore: https://ec.europ
 a.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/opportunities/topic-
 search?keywords=CERV-2026-CITIZENS-REM&utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantde
 sk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://ec.europa.eu/info/funding-tenders/opportunities/portal/screen/o
 pportunities/topic-search?keywords=CERV-2026-CITIZENS-REM&utm_source=artif
 icialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:EU Member States (incl. OCTs) and CERV-associated countries. Lead 
 applicant must be a non-profit legal entity or international organisation.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:jan-van-eyck-residency-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261124T224215Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Jan van Eyck Academie Residency 2028 (Maastrich
 t\, 11 months)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Jan van Eyck Academie's
  general open call for its 2028 residency year: 30 to 32 artists\, curator
 s\, designers\, writers\, architects and other artistic researchers spend 
 11 months (15 January to 15 December 2028) in Maastricht\, across material
 -based and research-driven practices\, with access to the academy's labs a
 nd community.\n\nOrganisation: Jan van Eyck Academie\nLocation: Maastricht
 \, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settle in Maastricht an
 d register with the municipality (the academy applies for visas where rele
 vant).\nAward: Monthly stipend of EUR 1\,500 (EUR 2\,000 for participants 
 with children\; EUR 1\,500 per duo member or EUR 2\,500 combined for life 
 partners\; collectives up to EUR 4\,500 combined\, max three stipends)\, w
 ith rent including service costs deducted from the stipend. Plus a EUR 2\,
 000 annual working budget and a newly built\, furnished private studio apa
 rtment. Application fee EUR 65 excl. VAT (EUR 78.65 incl. VAT)\, waived fo
 r applicants from and living in OECD DAC-list countries\; enrolment fee fo
 r accepted participants EUR 2\,750 excl. VAT.\nDuration: 11 months\, 15 Ja
 nuary to 15 December 2028\; 30 to 32 positions\; selection outcome mid-May
  2027.\n\nMore: https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency
 -2028?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.janvaneyck.nl/calendar/apply-now-jve-residency-2028?utm_sou
 rce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Maastricht\, Netherlands. Open worldwide\; participants must settl
 e in Maastricht and register with the municipality (the academy applies fo
 r visas where relevant).
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mensch-maschine-visit-fellowship-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20261124T224215Z
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DTSTART:20261201T222900Z
DTEND:20261201T225900Z
SUMMARY:Deadline 23:59 CET: Mensch Maschine VISIT Residency Fellowship 2027
 : Energy Ghosts (E-WERK Luckenwalde / Akademie der Künste)
DESCRIPTION:Closes 01 Dec 2026 at 23:59 CET.\n\nThe Mensch Maschine VISIT R
 esidency Program is an annual fellowship offering four fully funded fellow
 ships to artists from around the world\, run by the JUNGE AKADEMIE of the 
 Akademie der Künste (Berlin) with VISIT\, the artist-in-residence program
 me of the E.ON Foundation\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujazdowski Castle Centr
 e for Contemporary Art (Warsaw).\n\nOrganisation: JUNGE AKADEMIE of the Ak
 ademie der Künste\, VISIT (E.ON Foundation)\, E-WERK Luckenwalde and Ujaz
 dowski Castle Centre for Contemporary Art\nLocation: E-WERK Luckenwalde\, 
 Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademie der Künste\, Berlin (1 fel
 low)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CCA in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to
  artists worldwide.\nAward: Four fully funded fellowships of EUR 20\,000 e
 ach\, intended for artist fees and production costs of a new project (rese
 arch and development\, travel\, materials and presentation costs)\, plus s
 tudio space and accommodation for the three-month residency.\nDuration: Ab
 out three months\, mid-August to mid-November 2027: retreat at Ujazdowski 
 Castle in Warsaw in mid-August\, then the residency at E-WERK Luckenwalde 
 or Akademie der Künste Berlin from late August\, ending with a symposium 
 at the Akademie der Künste on 5 and 6 November 2027. Fellows must be avai
 lable from 13 August to 10 November 2027 and live and work on site at leas
 t 75% of the time.\n\nMore: https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-m
 aschine-stipendium?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referr
 al
URL:https://adk.de/news/2026/10/open-call-mensch-maschine-stipendium?utm_so
 urce=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:E-WERK Luckenwalde\, Brandenburg\, Germany (3 fellows) and Akademi
 e der Künste\, Berlin (1 fellow)\, with a retreat at Ujazdowski Castle CC
 A in Warsaw\, Poland. Open to artists worldwide.
END:VEVENT
